---
import ThemeButton from "../components/ThemeButton.astro";

const title = "Hardhat";
const description = "Hardhat's description";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <style>
      /* Minimal theming example using data-theme */
      :root {
        --bg: #ffffff;
        --fg: #0c0c0c;
      }
      html[data-theme="dark"] {
        --bg: #0b0b0e;
        --fg: #e7e7ea;
      }
      body {
        background: var(--bg);
        color: var(--fg);
        margin: 0;
        font:
          500 16px/1.5 system-ui,
          sans-serif;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Hardhat</h1>
    <p>
      This page is almost fully independent from the docs site, so we can
      implement the landing here however we want.
    </p>

    <h2>Synchronized theme selection</h2>
    <p>
      The only thing to keep in sync is the theme selection, otherwise it would
      be annoying to have two settings. I prototyped an implementation of this,
      which is functional but not styled.
    </p>
    <ThemeButton size={22} />
    <h2>Docs site</h2>
    <p>
      Just a link to navigate to the docs site:
      <a href="/docs/getting-started">Getting started</a>
    </p>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  html,
  body {
    margin: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }
</style>
